From 1a3cb34daf4f889003a1e66098b4f7c4253dc7fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:22:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix desktop layout: remove unlayered global
 margin/padding reset

The `* { margin: 0; padding: 0 }` rule in index.css is unlayered, so it
overrides Tailwind v4's layered utilities and disables mx-auto, p-*, m-*
etc. Tailwind's preflight already provides the reset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FcUgiTSjs6E9gyZtXP2C39
---
 src/index.css | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/index.css b/src/index.css
index 75a31a9..a457ead 100644
--- a/src/index.css
+++ b/src/index.css
@@ -23,11 +23,10 @@
 
 /* ===== Base Styles ===== */
 
-* {
-  margin: 0;
-  padding: 0;
-  box-sizing: border-box;
-}
+/* Tailwind's preflight already resets margin/padding/box-sizing inside
+   @layer base. Don't redeclare an unlayered `* { margin:0; padding:0 }` here:
+   unlayered CSS beats Tailwind v4's layered utilities and silently disables
+   every mx-auto, p-*, m-*, gap-adjacent spacing class. */
 
 html {
   scroll-behavior: smooth;
-- 
2.43.0


